# Residential Construction Project

## UTS 49002 – Managing Projects

**Project Type:** Residential Construction
**Project Context:** Project planning and management
**Role:** Quality Assurance
**Team:** Tutorial 7, Group 6
**Institution:** University of Technology Sydney (UTS)
**Semester:** Autumn 2025

---

## Project Overview

This project involved developing a comprehensive project management plan for the construction of a four-bedroom retirement home in Forster, New South Wales.

The project required the team to apply project management principles across the project lifecycle, including scope definition, scheduling, risk management, resource and cost planning, quality management, stakeholder management, communications, and project governance.

The project was developed as part of **UTS 49002 – Managing Projects**.

---

## My Role

I was assigned the role of **Quality Assurance** within the project team.

My responsibilities focused on reviewing project documentation for quality, consistency, accuracy, and integration across the team's deliverables.

My documented QA activities included:

* Reviewing project documentation for consistency and completeness
* Checking tables and project information against source material
* Reviewing document formatting and structure
* Checking references and APA 7 formatting
* Reviewing spelling and grammar
* Supporting version control through OneDrive
* Reviewing the project schedule and checking duration accuracy
* Conducting final document reviews before submission
* Supporting the integration of individual team members' work into the final project documentation

---

## Project Management Areas

The project required consideration of several interconnected project-management areas:

| Area                   | Application                                                                            |
| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Scope Management       | Definition of project objectives, deliverables, assumptions, exclusions and boundaries |
| Schedule Management    | Project activities, dependencies, durations and Gantt Chart                            |
| Risk Management        | Identification, assessment, treatment and monitoring of project risks                  |
| Resource Management    | Allocation of human resources and project responsibilities                             |
| Cost Management        | Project resource and cost planning                                                     |
| Quality Management     | Quality checks, document consistency and deliverable review                            |
| Stakeholder Management | Identification and consideration of project stakeholders                               |
| Communications         | Team communication, meetings and documentation                                         |
| Governance             | Defined responsibilities, documentation and project controls                           |
| Version Control        | Management of document revisions and collaborative project files                       |

